{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3245","id":3620312479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887XyZWf","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3245","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3245.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3245.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3245","number":3245,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"policy: implement nodeAttrs support","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #2319\n\nThis PR adds support for `nodeAttrs` in the Tailscale ACL policy, allowing operators to attach arbitrary capabilities to nodes via the policy file. These capabilities are distributed to clients through the CapMap field in MapResponse, enabling Tailscale client-side features that depend on node attributes.\n\n## What is implemented\n\n- **HuJSON parsing**: `nodeAttrs` array is parsed from the policy file alongside existing `acls` and `grants`.\n- **Target matching**: Supports user emails, tags (`tag:server`), IP addresses (IPv4/IPv6), and wildcard (`*`).\n- **Tag ownership semantics**: Respects the existing \"tags XOR user ownership\" rule—tagged nodes are owned by `TaggedDevices`, not the creating user.\n- **CapMap distribution**: Compiled `NodeCapMap` is included in `MapResponse` for all affected nodes on policy changes.\n- **Self-node invalidation**: When a policy change affects nodeAttrs, the mapper correctly invalidates the self node so clients receive updated CapMap without reconnecting.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n- `hscontrol/policy/v2/nodeattrs_test.go`: Unit tests for all target types (user, tag, IP, wildcard) and multiple-grant merge semantics.\n- `hscontrol/servertest/nodeattrs_test.go`: End-to-end server-level tests verifying CapMap appears in Netmap after policy reload.\n- `integration/nodeattrs_test.go`: Docker-based E2E tests verifying real tailscale clients receive and apply nodeAttrs dynamically.\n- `BenchmarkCompileNodeAttrs`: Micro-benchmark for regression tracking of CapMap compilation cost.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- Old clients (CapVer < 81) ignore CapMap; behavior is unchanged.\n- Policies without `nodeAttrs` behave exactly as before.\n- No database migration required.\n\n## Future work (out of scope)\n\nSome nodeAttrs require server-side features beyond CapMap distribution (e.g., `ippool` in #2912). This PR only covers the \"string-only\" CapMap path.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-05-03T15:05:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T17:39:24Z","closed_at":"2026-05-05T17:39:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5e9834569c7984867f2422d02ade53475ef7b4f5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us